63
00:03:47,120 --> 00:03:51,640
Scoutmaster ship in seven minutes or less.

64
00:03:59,920 --> 00:04:01,840
Well, there are four steps to scout advancement:

65
00:04:01,840 --> 00:04:07,280
A scout learns, a scout is tested, a scout is reviewed and a scout is recognized.

66
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:13,560
And in this podcast we're going to discuss step number three: a scout is reviewed.

67
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:18,839
Now, after a scouts completed all the requirements for any rank, he's reviewed

68
00:04:18,959 --> 00:04:24,880
twice. That's right, twice, because he is reviewed once in a Scoutmaster

69
00:04:24,880 --> 00:04:27,720
conference and once at a border review.

70
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:31,400
So let's start out by talking about the Scoutmaster conference,

71
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:37,080
And I've got a couple of resources to share with you from the Guide to

72
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:43,000
Advancement 2011.. In section four it talks about the unit

73
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,640
leader or Scoutmaster conference,

74
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:49,480
And it says: note that a scout must participate or take part in a conference.

75
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:55,480
It is not a test. Requirements do not say he must pass a conference.

76
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:59,200
Well, it makes sense to hold a conference after other requirements for a rank

77
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:04,280
or met. It is not required that it be the last step before the board of review.

78
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:09,520
The conference can provide a forum for discussing ambitions and life

79
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:13,080
purpose and for establishing goals for future achievement,

80
00:05:13,719 --> 00:05:19,200
But work left to be completed may be discussed just as easily as what is finished.

81
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:23,320
And then, if we go to the Scoutmaster handbook and read the section

82
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:25,479
about the Scoutmaster conference, we'll find this:

83
00:05:25,799 --> 00:05:29,400
The Scoutmaster conference is a visit between the Scoutmaster and a scout

84
00:05:29,760 --> 00:05:32,760
Held each time the boy completes the requirements for a rank.

85
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:36,680
It's a valuable opportunity to discuss his activity in the troop and his

86
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:40,080
understanding and practice of the ideals of scouting.

87
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:44,600
Together they can set goals not only in scouting, but also in his family,

88
00:05:44,600 --> 00:05:48,840
school and community. A scout taking part in a Scoutmaster conference

89
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:52,200
will be able to determine if he's ready to go before the board of review.

90
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:57,200
The Scoutmaster can also encourage a boy's advancement in scouting

91
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,600
by reviewing with him the requirements for his next rank.

92
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:05,640
The Scoutmaster conference can be used as a counseling tool at any time

93
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:09,840
and for a variety of other reasons. So, to begin with, put yourself in the

94
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:13,719
scout's shoes. A scout is going to be a little apprehensive about

95
00:06:13,719 --> 00:06:17,080
something called a Scoutmaster conference. right,

96
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:20,000
He's going to look in his book and he's going to say, my gosh,

97
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,479
I wonder what's going to happen next. I mean, how would we feel

98
00:06:23,479 --> 00:06:27,400
if the boss summoned us to a supervisors conference? or if we were

99
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:31,000
a student, we got summoned to a teachers conference at school?

100
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:33,680
Probably be a little apprehensive about either of those things.

101
00:06:33,680 --> 00:06:37,400
So we need to think about that. I'll bet that most scouts are not

102
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:41,280
looking forward to the Scoutmaster conference requirement. in the same

103
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:44,040
way, they are looking forward to fulfilling other requirements,

104
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:46,680
you know, like building a fire or cooking or camping. right,

105
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,400
What's going to happen? What is this old man going to ask me?

106
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,920
What if I don't know the right answers?

107
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:58,880
So our first task as Scoutmasters is putting the scouts at ease

108
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:02,920
and making sure that they understand that this is just a conference.

109
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:06,120
This is- this is just a visit that you and I are having

110
00:07:06,520 --> 00:07:08,320
so that we can talk about scouting,

111
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:11,480
And to do that, we're going to want to ask good, open-ended

112
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:15,040
questions that require more than a yes or no answer, even though

113
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:18,720
you may not get much more than a yes or no to begin with.

114
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:20,480
But you know, give it a try.

115
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:24,120
I think another really important aspect is the time

116
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:26,280
that we spend in a conference.

117
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:30,280
I think that you know 10 or 15 minutes is an eternity

118
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,640
when you're a boy,

119
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,919
So keep an eye on the clock.

120
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:37,200
So, within the Scoutmaster Conference, what we want to do

121
00:07:37,599 --> 00:07:40,360
is further establish the trust and understanding

122
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,080
between the scout and a Scoutmaster.

123
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:44,080
A conference, this is a give and take.

124
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:48,360
This is not something where we're dictating things to the scout.

125
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:51,800
This is something where we have a visit, where we talk.

126
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:55,159
We want to reinforce the ideals of scouting.

127
00:07:55,599 --> 00:07:58,360
You know there's there's a lot of great questions

128
00:07:58,360 --> 00:08:02,000
you can ask about school and home and family and church

129
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:05,840
and things that will just give you an idea of whether

130
00:08:05,840 --> 00:08:09,160
or not a scout is weaving the concepts of the Scout

131
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,000
oath and law into his life.

132
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:13,800
And you know, another important goal of a conference

133
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:16,720
is letting the scout and the Scoutmaster share ideas

134
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:18,320
and ask questions of one another.

135
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:21,000
I like to ask about school and what they like in school

136
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,320
and what they don't like in school.

137
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:25,040
It kind of gives me an idea of the boy's character

138
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,840
and what he may like about scouts.

139
00:08:26,960 --> 00:08:31,080
And then one of the other goals of course is collaborating

140
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:35,480
with the scout to set goals and outline steps for achieving them.

141
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:38,520
Like I said, a tender foot through life rank

142
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:43,320
Scoutmaster Conference. rule of thumb: 10 or 15 minutes at the most.

143
00:08:43,600 --> 00:08:46,600
Eagle Scout Scoutmaster Conferences might last a bit longer,

144
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:49,080
maybe up to 30 minutes.

145
00:08:49,080 --> 00:08:51,720
You want to make sure that we're giving the scout

146
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,600
our undivided attention.

147
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:56,360
We need to be in full view of others,

148
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:59,880
But we also need to be in a place where we can really hear

149
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:01,960
and understand what is being said.

150
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:04,640
And those open ended questions are an invitation

151
00:09:04,640 --> 00:09:06,320
for the scout to share

152
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:09,120
And we have to be really good listeners. with that,

153
00:09:09,120 --> 00:09:11,720
I contend to filibuster a Scoutmaster Conference

154
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,720
if I'm not careful.

155
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:17,040
So I have to be very intentional about listening to answers

156
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:19,560
and not jumping right in and offering advice

157
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:22,640
or reflection on what the scout just said,

158
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,440
but just really listening.

159
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,520
There's really no set place in time

160
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:28,040
for a Scoutmaster Conference.

161
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,520
You can do these at troop meetings or outdoor activities

162
00:09:30,520 --> 00:09:32,760
or any time you have an opportunity.

163
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:36,600
Like I said, we always follow youth protection guidelines.

164
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:40,880
So while this is a one on one conference with a scout,

165
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,480
we're always in full view of other adults and scouts.

166
00:09:43,480 --> 00:09:47,160
Another really important aspect is keeping the tone positive.

167
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:49,400
Occasionally you'll have a Scoutmaster Conference

168
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:51,680
with somebody who has some behavioral issues

169
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:55,400
or attitude problems or things like that,

170
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:59,160
And if a scout needs to improve on those things,

171
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:02,200
be sure to bring up behavior and achievements

172
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:03,840
that you can praise too.

173
00:10:03,840 --> 00:10:07,240
Scouts will hear criticism a lot louder sometimes

174
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,680
than they will hear praise.

175
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:10,280
You know, when we read the quote

176
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:12,600
from the Guide to Advancement,

177
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,920
it was specific in that scouts don't pass

178
00:10:15,920 --> 00:10:17,960
a Scoutmaster Conference,

179
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:20,640
So they don't fail them either.

180
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:23,120
Once we've conducted a conference with a scout,

181
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:27,480
that requirement for his rank is completed.

182
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,240
Now let's say we conduct the conference

183
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:31,840
and we discover that there's a requirement

184
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,560
that's not been signed off,

185
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:35,400
that we're not going to complete

186
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:37,240
in the course of the conference,

187
00:10:37,240 --> 00:10:40,280
or there's a behavioral or attitude issue

188
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:43,360
or something like that that needs to be dealt with.

189
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:46,160
You're going to collaborate with the scout.

190
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:48,800
You're going to find out from him

191
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:51,000
what he thinks needs to be done

192
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:52,680
to remedy the difficulty,

193
00:10:52,680 --> 00:10:55,760
And then you're going to set some concrete ways

194
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:58,000
for that to happen and schedule a time

195
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,960
to talk again and follow up.

196
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:01,920
And that way you're kind of pausing

197
00:11:01,920 --> 00:11:03,280
the Scoutmaster Conference

198
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:04,840
and then you're going to pick it up again

199
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:05,800
And in the meantime

200
00:11:05,800 --> 00:11:08,320
you're going to do everything you possibly can

201
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:10,760
to help the scout remedy these difficulties.

202
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:14,520
So the conferences are collaborative.

203
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:17,320
This is not just a simple evaluation

204
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:19,480
and a passing of judgment.

205
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,840
This is a discussion.

206
00:11:20,840 --> 00:11:22,160
You can learn a lot about the scout

207
00:11:22,160 --> 00:11:24,080
and his experience in his troop and patrol.

208
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,680
that will help inform

209
00:11:25,680 --> 00:11:27,640
the way that we present the program.

210
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:30,440
Properly done, a Scoutmaster's Conference

211
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,720
is an overwhelmingly positive experience for the scout.

212
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:35,680
Even if he's found himself in a tight spot

213
00:11:35,680 --> 00:11:38,280
because behavior performance is causing him problems,

214
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,320
he ought to leave the conference

215
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:43,680
encouraged, energized and happy.

216
00:11:43,680 --> 00:11:46,120
Now, if you go to scoutmastercgcom

217
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,640
and follow the link in the post

218
00:11:47,640 --> 00:11:49,520
that contains this podcast,

219
00:11:49,520 --> 00:11:52,360
you'll find a PDF resource I created.

220
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:54,880
that's just kind of a one-page set of notes

221
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,680
about Scoutmaster Conferences.

222
00:11:56,680 --> 00:12:01,120
So we said that scouts are reviewed twice

223
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:04,160
and the next time that that's going to happen

224
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:07,040
is something called the Board of Review.

225
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:10,280
So let's go to the resources on this.

226
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:13,400
In the Scoutmaster Handbook. it says this:

227
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:15,840
the purpose of the Board of Review

228
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:18,840
is not to retest a scout,

229
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:21,120
but rather to ensure that he has completed

230
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:23,360
all the requirements, to determine the quality

231
00:12:23,360 --> 00:12:25,280
of his troop experience and to encourage him

232
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:27,120
to advance towards the next rank.

233
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:30,640
Every review should also include a discussion of ways

234
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:32,720
in which the scout sees himself

235
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:35,240
as living up to the scout oath and law

236
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,439
in his everyday life,

237
00:12:36,439 --> 00:12:39,360
And then from the guide to advancement.

238
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:41,360
the one reason for a Board of Review

239
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:44,600
is to ensure that the scout did what he was supposed to do

240
00:12:44,600 --> 00:12:46,240
to meet the requirements.

241
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:50,520
It shall become neither a retest or examination

242
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:53,440
nor a challenge of his knowledge.

243
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:55,760
In most cases it should instead

244
00:12:55,760 --> 00:12:58,120
be a celebration of accomplishment.

245
00:12:58,120 --> 00:13:01,080
Remember, it is more about the journey.

246
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:04,680
A badge recognizes what a young man is able to do

247
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,320
and how he has grown.

248
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:09,360
It is not so much a reward for what he has done.

249
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:12,480
So why isn't a Board of Review

250
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:15,400
a test or a challenge of the scout's knowledge?

251
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,400
The simple answer is:

252
00:13:16,400 --> 00:13:18,920
is he has any number of signatures as evidence

253
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:21,280
that he has been tested and passed

254
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,840
on the required skills and knowledge?

255
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,960
I mean, he has that part of his handbook

256
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:26,520
with all the requirements listed.

257
00:13:26,520 --> 00:13:28,840
they're checked and they're signed and dated,

258
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:29,840
He's been tested.

259
00:13:29,840 --> 00:13:31,040
Another important thing is

260
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:32,800
is that the object of the Board of Review

261
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:35,920
is far more important than a test or an examination.

262
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:38,400
The purpose of a Board of Review

263
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:42,079
isn't to determine the quality of a scout's work.

264
00:13:42,079 --> 00:13:46,560
It's to gauge the quality of his experience in scouting.

265
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:49,120
So, going back to the last podcast

266
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,600
when we talked about a scout is tested,

267
00:13:51,600 --> 00:13:54,079
we only have one opportunity to determine

268
00:13:54,079 --> 00:13:56,079
if a scout has the prerequisite skill

269
00:13:56,079 --> 00:13:57,720
to pass a requirement,

270
00:13:57,720 --> 00:13:59,840
And that happens when he's tested.

271
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,480
A scout's knowledge or skill

272
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,760
is going to be challenged many times

273
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:07,319
in the natural course of doing what scouts do,

274
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:10,560
But he's only going to be tested and passed

275
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:14,200
and have that requirement signed off once.

276
00:14:14,200 --> 00:14:16,680
When he's successfully completed the test,

277
00:14:16,680 --> 00:14:18,640
it's certified by a signature.

278
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:20,360
he's not going to be tested

279
00:14:20,360 --> 00:14:22,720
on that particular requirement again.

280
00:14:22,720 --> 00:14:25,760
So the question of his qualification to advance

281
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:28,000
as far as the requirements are concerned

282
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,360
is seeing that his book is signed.

283
00:14:30,360 --> 00:14:33,280
The question of the quality of his experience

284
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,160
is discussing the journey

285
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:38,040
he took to get those signatures.

286
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:39,800
Think about it this way.

287
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,800
Let's say the scouts just arrived home

288
00:14:41,800 --> 00:14:44,120
from a long journey overseas.

289
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,560
The signatures in his handbook

290
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:47,400
are like an album of pictures

291
00:14:47,400 --> 00:14:48,959
that he took along the way.

292
00:14:48,959 --> 00:14:50,040
If we look at the pictures,

293
00:14:50,040 --> 00:14:51,800
we know where he went and what he did,

294
00:14:51,800 --> 00:14:53,520
but we really don't know much

295
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:57,360
about how he experienced the journey.

296
00:14:57,360 --> 00:15:00,880
So we pose questions that ask about the journey

297
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:02,560
You know. tell us about the camping trip

298
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:03,560
where you're the patrol cook.

299
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:04,560
How did that go?

300
00:15:04,560 --> 00:15:06,400
Can you point out one thing that you think

301
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:10,360
was the most important thing you've learned thus far?

302
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,320
Tell us about the people that you traveled with.

303
00:15:12,320 --> 00:15:13,320
What's your patrol like?

304
00:15:13,320 --> 00:15:14,440
How do you like it?

305
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:16,640
How's everything going for you in the troop?

306
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,760
Do you understand what goes on?

307
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:20,640
Do you think the troop meetings are useful?

308
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,480
Did you enjoy the camp out?

309
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:24,000
Questions like that.

310
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,960
Now a board that actively listens

311
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:28,480
to the answers to those types of questions

312
00:15:28,480 --> 00:15:31,080
will learn about how the scout understands

313
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:33,120
and experiences the journey,

314
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:35,400
what might be causing him problems

315
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:38,480
and also the strengths and weaknesses

316
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:39,960
of the troops program.

317
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:42,160
So the board of review is not so much

318
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:44,400
a critical evaluation of the scout

319
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:47,640
as it is a critical examination of the program

320
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:49,120
he's traveled through.

321
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,960
Properly managed boards of review

322
00:15:50,960 --> 00:15:53,800
are a terrifically powerful look

323
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:55,920
into how well we're doing,

324
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:58,400
how well the program is being presented.

325
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:01,840
Just like going to a scout master conference.

326
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,840
a scout will probably be nervous

327
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:06,720
about going to a board of review.

328
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:09,280
That little term is going to pop up out of the book,

329
00:16:09,280 --> 00:16:12,320
and it can be pretty daunting for some scouts,

330
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:14,000
especially when they're going

331
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,680
to their first or second board of review, right.

332
00:16:16,680 --> 00:16:20,000
So the atmosphere at the board can be formal,

333
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,760
but it ought to be very relaxed.

334
00:16:21,760 --> 00:16:23,600
The members of the board should make a point

335
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,520
out of putting the scout at ease

336
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:27,000
and making sure that he understands

337
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:29,520
the intention of the board of review.

338
00:16:29,520 --> 00:16:30,760
I don't want to talk a lot

339
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:33,960
about the precise mechanics of a board of review,

340
00:16:33,960 --> 00:16:37,400
because they're discussed in detail very thoroughly

341
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:40,920
in the Guide to Advancement 2011 in section eight.

342
00:16:40,920 --> 00:16:42,160
Before we close this out, though,

343
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:45,199
I will go over four things

344
00:16:45,199 --> 00:16:47,720
that are said in the Guide to Advancement

345
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:50,079
that are often misunderstood.

346
00:16:50,079 --> 00:16:52,880
First, a scout can't be denied the opportunity

347
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,560
to have a board of review

348
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:56,640
If he believes he's completed all the requirements,

349
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:58,640
including a scout master conference.

350
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:01,600
it's up to the unit leader and the committee

351
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,000
to assure a board of review is held.

352
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:08,280
We don't have the authority to expect a boy

353
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:11,639
to request one, or defer to him,

354
00:17:11,639 --> 00:17:15,440
or ask him to perform beyond the requirements

355
00:17:15,440 --> 00:17:18,119
in order to be granted a board of review.

356
00:17:18,119 --> 00:17:21,800
Boards of review consist of no fewer than three

357
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:23,839
and no more than six members

358
00:17:23,839 --> 00:17:26,960
and unit leaders, like scout masters

359
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:29,440
and assistant scout masters, cannot serve

360
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:33,240
on the board of review for a scout in their own unit.

361
00:17:33,240 --> 00:17:36,200
Parents or guardians may not serve on a board

362
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,680
for their son,

363
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:40,040
The candidate, or his parents or guardians

364
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:43,280
shall have no part in selecting any members

365
00:17:43,280 --> 00:17:44,920
for the board of review either.

366
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:48,600
Here's one that causes a lot of needed trouble sometimes.

367
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:53,240
is preferred a scout being full field uniform

368
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:54,800
for any board of review?

369
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:57,200
He should wear as much of it as he owns

370
00:17:57,200 --> 00:18:00,080
and it should be correct as possible

371
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,879
with the badges worn properly.

372
00:18:02,879 --> 00:18:06,600
Can we just go back there and note some of the words

373
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:11,600
preferred? should, should, as possible. okay,

374
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:16,360
If wearing all or part of the uniform

375
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:19,520
is impractical for whatever reason,

376
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:22,600
the candidate should be clean and neat in his appearance

377
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:25,880
and dressed appropriately according to his means

378
00:18:25,880 --> 00:18:29,160
for the milestone marked by the occasion.

379
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:32,680
Regardless of unit expectations or rules,

380
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:36,200
boards of review may not reject candidates

381
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:38,560
dressed to this description.

382
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:41,480
Neither may they require the purchase of uniforming

383
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:44,120
or clothing such as coats and ties.

384
00:18:44,120 --> 00:18:46,000
So that particular rule

385
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:47,960
that might be a surprise to some of us.

386
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:50,120
It was a surprise to me. okay,

387
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:53,760
A uniform is not required for a board of review,

388
00:18:53,760 --> 00:18:57,440
It's preferred, but if it's impractical, for whatever reason,

389
00:18:57,440 --> 00:18:59,760
the candidate should be clean and neat in his appearance

390
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:04,760
and, regardless of any rules or expectations we may have,

391
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:08,120
boards of review can't reject candidates

392
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:10,240
if they're dressed to that description.

393
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:12,800
Finally, the unit leader can remain in the room,

394
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:15,520
but only to observe and not to participate

395
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:16,880
unless called upon.

396
00:19:16,880 --> 00:19:20,200
The scout's parents, relatives or guardians

397
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:22,800
may not be in attendance in any capacity,

398
00:19:22,800 --> 00:19:25,320
not as members of the board, as observers

399
00:19:25,320 --> 00:19:27,360
or even as the unit leader.

400
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:30,320
Their presence can change discussion dynamics.

401
00:19:30,320 --> 00:19:33,000
Now, if you go and you read in the Guide to Advancement,

402
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:34,640
of course in scouting

403
00:19:34,640 --> 00:19:39,640
we have nothing where we absolutely exclude

404
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:41,320
parents from observing.

405
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:45,920
And if a parent insists on observing the board of review

406
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:48,080
and after we've spoken to them about it

407
00:19:48,080 --> 00:19:51,160
and explained that there's a lot of people in there

408
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:53,720
and we don't have parents or guardians

409
00:19:53,720 --> 00:19:56,120
in a board of review normally

410
00:19:56,120 --> 00:19:58,200
because we think that their presence

411
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:00,720
can change the dynamics of the discussion.

412
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:03,200
But if you insist, you may certainly sit in

413
00:20:03,200 --> 00:20:04,440
as an observer.

414
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,920
You'll find that in the Guide to Advancement.

415
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:08,400
You'll find it a very well written

416
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:10,600
and concise set of directions

417
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:13,400
on holding boards of review in the Guide to Advancement.

418
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:16,160
So next time. we're gonna close this series up

419
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:18,560
with step number four,

420
00:20:18,560 --> 00:20:21,600
and that is a Scout is Running Man.

421
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:24,600
["Scout is Running Man"].

422
00:20:30,640 --> 00:20:32,560
Hi, I'm Kevin Callan and I'm listening

423
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,280
to Scoutmaster iPod.

424
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:35,600
No, I can't.

425
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,880
What is it called again?

426
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,240
Hi, I'm Kevin Callan, the happy camper,

427
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:45,880
and you're listening to the Scoutmaster podcast.

428
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,040
Ah, beautiful.

429
00:20:47,040 --> 00:20:50,040
["Scout Master"]

430
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:06,200
Email. that is, folks,

431
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:09,320
And here's an answer to one of your emails.

432
00:21:14,160 --> 00:21:17,160
["Scout Master"].

433
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,600
I had this email come in this week.

434
00:21:18,600 --> 00:21:21,160
I'm interested to do your advice on record keeping.

435
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:24,280
Our troop currently keeps no advancement records

436
00:21:24,280 --> 00:21:26,560
on any Scout and expects the Scout

437
00:21:26,560 --> 00:21:28,640
to maintain their own records.

438
00:21:28,640 --> 00:21:29,880
This came to a head recently

439
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:33,360
when one of our young Scouts lost a blue card.

440
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:36,120
The response he received was: you know, that's tough.

441
00:21:36,120 --> 00:21:38,600
You'll have to redo the merit badge.

442
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:41,760
This is part of becoming a Scout.

443
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:44,360
I think there are better ways and methods

444
00:21:44,360 --> 00:21:47,440
to teach responsibility than that.

445
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:49,200
Do you have any suggestions?

446
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:51,120
Not only are there better ways and methods

447
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:52,760
to teach responsibility,

448
00:21:52,760 --> 00:21:54,400
we've got a couple of things happening here

449
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,960
that aren't pointed at true north.

450
00:21:55,960 --> 00:21:57,600
Let's deal with them one at a time.

451
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,040
If you go to the Guide to Advancement,

452
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:02,520
you're going to find a list of unit

453
00:22:02,520 --> 00:22:04,840
advancement committee responsibilities,

454
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:07,040
and one of them is keeping records.

455
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:10,800
The idea that Scouts have to keep these records

456
00:22:10,800 --> 00:22:12,280
and maintain them by themselves

457
00:22:12,280 --> 00:22:15,760
and if they screw up or they lose a blue card

458
00:22:15,760 --> 00:22:16,600
or something like that,

459
00:22:16,600 --> 00:22:20,080
well, we're teaching responsibility through tough love

460
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:22,320
and that's just too bad for them.

461
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:25,320
I can see that that is kind of right in theory,

462
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:27,960
but it is absolutely wrong in practice.

463
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:29,960
You know, a Scout maintains his handbook

464
00:22:29,960 --> 00:22:31,800
and he has the signatures and things in it

465
00:22:31,800 --> 00:22:33,600
and every once in a while

466
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:35,879
a Scout loses his handbook and we got to go back

467
00:22:35,879 --> 00:22:40,080
and see if we can recreate the signatures that he had

468
00:22:40,120 --> 00:22:42,439
and if we're keeping records on. that

469
00:22:42,439 --> 00:22:43,720
makes it really easy.

470
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,800
If a Scout loses a blue card,

471
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:48,320
all he has to do is get back in touch with a counselor

472
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,760
and say: you know, I'm very sorry,

473
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:50,879
I kind of screwed up here.

474
00:22:50,879 --> 00:22:52,840
I lost the blue card.

475
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:54,800
I know you maintain the part of the blue card

476
00:22:54,800 --> 00:22:57,520
that represents that I completed the badge

477
00:22:57,520 --> 00:22:59,159
and if it'd be okay with you,

478
00:22:59,159 --> 00:23:00,399
I'd like to come and visit you

479
00:23:00,399 --> 00:23:04,320
and I'd like to get you to sign a new blue card.

480
00:23:04,320 --> 00:23:05,960
There's enough trouble in that

481
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:07,840
that the Scout's going to remember

482
00:23:07,879 --> 00:23:10,360
not to lose a blue card the next time, right?

483
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:12,439
This is a real good example of something that

484
00:23:12,439 --> 00:23:14,560
you know theoretically sounds great-

485
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:16,159
teaching the boys responsibility

486
00:23:16,159 --> 00:23:17,639
and everything like that-

487
00:23:17,639 --> 00:23:21,040
but if that was a good way to do it,

488
00:23:21,040 --> 00:23:23,240
if that was what was intended in the program,

489
00:23:23,240 --> 00:23:24,959
we'd find it in the guide to advancement,

490
00:23:24,959 --> 00:23:28,159
and we don't actually, we find quite the opposite.

491
00:23:28,159 --> 00:23:30,280
So I hope that helped

492
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:32,159
and you can get in touch with me

493
00:23:32,159 --> 00:23:34,080
with your email questions

494
